  "contentHtml": "\n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p>Bengaluru: Blackstone-owned AGS Health on Friday filed updated draft papers for a 48-billion-rupee ($504 million) <a href=\"/tag/initial+public+offering\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">initial public offering</a> in India, nearly two months after securing the markets regulator's approval ‌for a ⁠listing.⁠The IPO consists of a fresh issue of shares worth up to 18 billion rupees, and <a href=\"/tag/blackstone\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Blackstone</a> selling shares worth up to 30 billion rupees.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>AGS Health had confidentially ​filed for an IPO ⁠with the ‌Securities and Exchange Board ​of India (SEBI) ​in April, with the proposed ⁠listing valuing the company at about $3 ​billion, Bloomberg News had reported.</p>\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>​The confidential route allows companies to submit draft papers with the regulator for feedback without making the details public, giving them greater flexibility on ‌timing and disclosure.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>The company is a revenue cycle management (RCM) provider ​that helps ​U.S. hospitals ⁠and healthcare providers manage billing, insurance claims and payments.For the year ended March 31, ​AGS Health posted a profit of 2.07 billion rupees and a revenue of 20.41 billion rupees, draft papers showed.                    </p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                       